course: dictionary
lesson: 8422
title: Rustle: a sound, a snack and a clue
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «The dry leaves rustled in the wind» is about a soft, crackling sound. «We can rustle up a snack» uses rustle to mean make something quickly. Read the words around it first.
explain: «Something rustled in the bushes.» In a story, a rustle like this builds suspense, because you wonder what is hiding there. In a science lesson, rustle is just a sound word, like whisper or crunch.
explain: Watch for the phrase «cattle rustler». The word cattle is the clue. It means a thief who steals cattle, as in old Western stories. Here rustle has nothing to do with a sound.
fact: To rustle is to make a soft, light, crackling sound, like dry leaves or paper moving.
fact: A rustle is that sound, as in «the rustle of leaves».
fact: «Rustle up» means to make or find something quickly, like a quick snack.
fact: To rustle cattle means to steal them, as in old Western stories.
fact: Rustling wrappers in a cinema is noisy and spoils the film for others, so eat quietly.
exercise: «The dry leaves rustled as the fox crept past.» What does rustled mean here? | Made a soft, crackling sound | *Stole the leaves | Turned bright red | Fell down very quickly
exercise: Mum says, «Let's rustle up some lunch from what is in the fridge.» What does rustle up mean? | Throw the food away | Wash all the dishes slowly | *Make or find something quickly | Go shopping for a whole week
exercise: «The cattle rustler rode away at dawn.» What is a cattle rustler? | A singer at the rodeo | A horse racer | *A thief who steals cattle | A farmer who feeds the cows
test: «At the cinema you eat quietly and do not rustle wrappers.» Why should you not rustle wrappers? | Because the cinema is closed | Because wrappers cannot be eaten | Because the wrappers are made of gold | *Because the noise spoils the film for other people
test: «The fox heard a rustle in the long grass.» What is a rustle in this sentence? | A type of grass | A big storm | *A soft sound | A kind of fox
exam: «Its ears gathered the tiny rustle of a vole in the long grass.» What is a rustle in this sentence? | A small animal | A kind of wind | *A tiny, soft sound | A loud crash
